<p>In this section, you will set up the connection pool, ensure your database schema is in place, and manage database connections effectively. To connect to your <code>PostgreSQL</code> database, you will use the <code>asyncpg</code> library for asynchronous database connections.</p>
<p>First, create a <code>.env</code> file in the root of your project to store the database connection URL. This file will hold environment-specific variables, such as the connection string to your Neon PostgreSQL database.</p>
